              "level": 0,
              "text": "significant bradyarrhythmias can develop.",
              "pdf_page": 320,
              "printed_page": 238,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "INTERACTIONS"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Systolic anterior motion of the mitral valve,",
              "pdf_page": 320,
              "printed_page": 238,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "INTERACTIONS"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Avoid potent arteriolar dilators in cases",
              "pdf_page": 320,
              "printed_page": 238,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "INTERACTIONS"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "suggesting dynamic LV outflow tract",
              "pdf_page": 320,
              "printed_page": 238,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "INTERACTIONS"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "with dynamic LVOTO. The use of milder",
              "pdf_page": 320,
              "printed_page": 238,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "INTERACTIONS"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "obstruction (LVOTO), is common in dogs",
              "pdf_page": 320,
              "printed_page": 238,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "INTERACTIONS"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "vasodilators such as ACE inhibitors in dogs",
              "pdf_page": 320,
              "printed_page": 238,
